berkeley-principles-4.logic.r1: argue/scope: A1: read with the necessity on its consequent alone, objects_are_perceived ∧ perceive_only_ideas → □(objects_unperceived → ideas_unperceived), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □(objects_are_perceived ∧ perceive_only_ideas → (objects_unperceived → ideas_unperceived)), C (S2) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
